  "title": "sesudah, setelah — after",
  "pattern": "A sesudah B · Setelah B, A · Sesudah itu, …",
  "explanation": "sesudah and setelah both mean after, and they work just like sebelum, followed by an action or a time: sesudah makan (after eating), setelah sarapan (after breakfast). They're interchangeable; setelah is a little more common in writing and announcements. Sesudah itu or setelah itu at the start of a sentence means after that. In casual speech the everyday after is habis: Habis makan, kita jalan-jalan, yuk.",
  "natural": "sesudah and setelah in any polite conversation, in instructions (diminum sesudah makan) and in plans. habis with friends and family.",
  "stiff": "habis to a stranger or someone senior can sound too casual. It also means finished or sold out (Nasinya habis — the rice has run out), so it needs context to mean after.",
